  "description": "This recipe can easily be scaled up or down, and if you have plastic squeeze bottles, there's no need to first whisk in a bowl—construct the dressing in the bottles using the same ratio and shake before each use.",
  "notes": "Notes: This recipe can easily be scaled up or down. If you have plastic squeeze bottles, there's no need to first whisk in a bowl—construct the dressing in the bottles using the same ratio of ingredients, scaling down to fit in one bottle. Cover the top and shake before each use.Note that if the garlic and shallot are not minced finely enough, they can clog the spout of a squeeze bottle. You can widen the spout by cutting it (the hole gets larger the closer you cut it to the bottle), but you should still endeavor to mince very finely, or grate with the Microplane.",
